# Bowerbird Plugin Store & Distribution Environment
#
# The desktop app has exactly ONE address: the plugin store origin, which serves
# the store front end plus the plugin API (/api/plugins/<id>/manifest.json,
# /api/plugins/<id>/download, /api/plugins/<id>/<file>). It is consumed at BUILD
# time - the platform Taskfiles link it into the binary (-X bowerbird/core.storeURL,
# see core/store.go) and ship no hardcoded host. Export it before
# `wails3 task <os>:package`, or set the PLUGIN_STORE_URL repository variable for
# the release workflow. The same variable in the app's own runtime environment
# overrides the injected value.

# Desktop app: plugin store origin. The local marketplace dev server runs at
# http://localhost:3000.
PLUGIN_STORE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Marketplace app (apps/marketplace/) only ---------------------------------
# Distribution repository the *store* pulls from; not compiled into the desktop app.

# Plugin index file in the distribution repository
PLUGIN_REPO_INDEX_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/owocc/bowerbird-plugins/main/index.min.json

# Release archives served/redirected by the store (<plugin-id>-<version>.zip)
PLUGIN_RELEASE_BASE_URL=https://github.com/owocc/bowerbird-plugins/releases/download/plugins-latest

# Optional: GitHub Personal Access Token for private repos or higher rate limits
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: marketplace index cache TTL in seconds (default 300)
PLUGIN_CACHE_TTL=300
